@startuml
!include ../../../../../../plantuml/sodexo-theme.puml

title Resolve a failed or uncertain booking — End-to-end interaction
header Sat, 25 Jul 2026 · End-to-end discovery sequence
footer (c) Developed by <b>Mohit Kanwar</b>

hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 90

actor "Booking Operator" as Actor
participant "Booking Operations Workspace" as Surface
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Accommodation Experience API" as Edge
participant "Booking.com Integration Service" as Service1
participant "Booking Workflow Service" as Service2
database "Service-owned data" as Data
queue "Kafka event platform" as Events
participant "Booking.com Demand API" as BookingCom #FBDADD


group 1. Query supplier state before deciding whether a retry is safe.
  Actor -> Surface: Query supplier state before deciding whether a retry is safe
  Surface -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/supplier-orders/details
  Gateway -> Edge: JWT, tenant scope, correlation ID
  Edge -> Service1: Query supplier state before deciding whether a retry is safe.
  alt authorised and valid
  Service1 -> Service1: Authorise and query
  Service1 -> BookingCom: POST /3.2/orders/details
  BookingCom --> Service1: Supplier response + request_id
  Service1 --> Edge: Scoped result
  Edge --> Surface: Response envelope
  Surface --> Actor: Updated journey state
else validation, state, or dependency failure
  Service1 --> Edge: Problem details + retryability
  Edge --> Surface: Safe error and next action
  Surface --> Actor: Correct, retry later, or escalate
end
end

group 2. Retry only after a conclusive absent result or an idempotent outcome.
  Actor -> Surface: Retry only after a conclusive absent result or an idempotent outcome
  Surface -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/booking-work-items/{workItemId}/retry
  Gateway -> Edge: JWT, tenant scope, correlation ID
  Edge -> Service2: Retry only after a conclusive absent result or an idempotent outcome.
  alt authorised and valid
  Service2 -> Service2: Validate transition and persist
  Service2 -> Data: Read or commit Booking Workflow Service data
  Service2 -> Events: Publish committed domain event
  Service2 --> Edge: Accepted state and next actions
  Edge --> Surface: Response envelope
  Surface --> Actor: Updated journey state
else validation, state, or dependency failure
  Service2 --> Edge: Problem details + retryability
  Edge --> Surface: Safe error and next action
  Surface --> Actor: Correct, retry later, or escalate
end
end

@enduml
